    "content": "I understand your frustration and the urgency of your situation. You're absolutely right - you need direct action from someone with the authority to make operational changes, not just documentation.\n\nHowever, I need to be transparent about my role here. I'm an AI assistant with access to the CRM system, but I don't have the ability to:\n- Connect you with account leadership\n- Make operational changes to your service\n- Guarantee specific service improvements\n- Override service delivery processes\n\nWhat I can do is help you:\n1. **Document everything** in the CRM so there's a clear record of your concerns and the recovery plan\n2. **Track the timeline** of your evaluation and decision deadline\n3. **Create a structured approach** for when you do connect with the right person\n\nGiven that you're in the final stages of evaluation with a 3-week deadline, and you've already lost two accounts due to these issues, this is a critical situation.\n\n**My recommendation:** You should contact your actual account manager or customer success team directly to:\n- Request a meeting with someone who has operational authority\n- Ask for a concrete remediation plan with specific timelines\n- Request written commitments for service level improvements\n- Understand what escalation paths exist for future issues\n\nWould you like me to:\n1. Update the existing \"Transition Corp Recovery\" opportunity to reflect the urgency (perhaps change the stage or add notes)?\n2. Create a task specifically to track your 3-week evaluation timeline?\n3. Help you prepare a list of specific questions to ask when you speak with your account leadership?\n\nI want to be helpful within my capabilities, but I cannot make the operational changes you need - that requires human account leadership with the appropriate authority.",
